WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:09.090
Getting the “side-eye” look from your dog can make it seem like they are making a judgement about you, and some new studies suggest they really could be.
自家狗狗“斜眼”看你时，你可能会觉得它好像在评判你，而一些新研究表明，它或许真的是在评判你。

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:17.160
The ability to judge others’ intentions is an indicator of possessing “theory of mind”, which was once thought to be unique to humans.
能够判断他人的意图，是具备“心理理论”的一个标志，而心理理论一度被认为是人类所独有的。

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:25.800
However, new studies have shown that dogs can read human behaviour and have a preference for people who are more friendly or generous with food.
然而，新研究表明，狗能够读懂人的行为，而且偏爱更友善或给吃的更大方的人。

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:36.380
One such study published in 2023 aimed to see if dogs can tell the difference between humans who are “unwilling” and those who are “unable” to give them a treat.
2023年发表的一项此类研究旨在弄清，狗能否区分“不愿意”给它们零食的人和“无法”给它们零食的人。

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:42.950
Ninety-six dogs were involved in both “unwilling” and “unable” scenarios designed for the study.
96只狗都参与了为这项研究设计的“不愿意”和“无法”两种情境的测试。

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:52.410
Both scenarios involved a dog being placed on one side of a glass screen with small holes in it at nose-height, and an experimenter standing on the other.
两种情境都是把一只狗安置在一块玻璃隔板的一侧，隔板上与狗鼻子齐高的位置开有一些小孔，一名实验者则站在隔板的另一侧。

00:00:53.210 --> 00:01:01.410
In the “unwilling” scenario, the experimenter would hang a piece of sausage in front of the screen in a “teasing” manner, and approach one of the holes.
在“不愿意”情境中，实验者会以“戏耍”的方式把一块香肠悬在隔板前，并靠近其中一个小孔。

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.850
But instead of passing it through the hole to the dog, they would then pull it out of the dog’s reach.
但实验者随后并没有把香肠从孔中递给狗，而是把它拿开，让狗够不着。

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:16.660
For the “unable” scenario, the experimenter would again move the treat towards the hole while the dog watched, but “accidentally” drop it before they could pass it through.
在“无法”情境中，实验者同样会在狗的注视下把零食移向小孔，但在递过去之前“不小心”让它掉了下去。

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:26.330
The researchers observed that the dogs were much more patient, making more eye contact and staying closer to the screen after the “unable” scenario played out.
研究人员观察到，“无法”情境结束后，狗要耐心得多：眼神交流更多，也待得离隔板更近。

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:35.100
In the “unwilling” scenario, however, the dogs looked at the experimenter less often and sat, lay down and wandered around more frequently.
然而在“不愿意”情境中，狗看实验者的次数更少，而坐下、趴下和四处走动则更频繁。

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:49.430
Another study from 2021 tested for “theory of mind” in dogs in a similar way, but the dogs were able to walk round the screen to obtain the treat after witnessing the experimenter’s “unwilling” or “unable” behaviour.
2021年的另一项研究以类似的方式检测狗是否具备“心理理论”，不过在这项研究中，狗在目睹实验者“不愿意”或“无法”的行为之后，可以绕过隔板去拿零食。

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:58.010
The main finding was that the dogs approached the experimenter significantly sooner in the unable scenario than in the unwilling scenario.
主要发现是：与“不愿意”情境相比，狗在“无法”情境中明显更早地走近实验者。

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:13.780
However, the researchers of the 2023 study argued that the food dropped on the floor in the clumsy manner might have motivated the dogs to approach the experimenter, considering that they probably often obtain food dropped on the floor in their daily lives.
不过，2023年那项研究的研究人员认为，考虑到狗在日常生活中很可能常常能吃到掉在地上的食物，实验者笨手笨脚弄掉在地上的食物可能是促使狗走近实验者的原因。

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:21.780
Now, more evidence has been provided that dogs distinguish between similar actions associated with different intentions.
如今，已有更多证据表明，狗会区分与不同意图相关的相似行为。

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:28.970
But how exactly they acquire such intention-reading abilities will be an exciting topic for future research.
但狗究竟是如何获得这种解读意图的能力的，将会是未来研究中一个令人兴奋的课题。
